add('N088','J. The final Tsen and coefficient-comparison leaf','The author’s true-isomorphism question',[(51,14),(51,19)],'self-flagged',r'“est-ce … un vrai isomorphisme?”; “mod p”',r'isomorph|roots|racines|torsion|divisib|cohomolog',r'''The margin questions the displayed comparison between roots-of-unity coefficients and multiplicative coefficients after a quotient described as uniquely divisible away from the characteristic. The relevant inclusion is \(U\hookrightarrow\widetilde K^*\); its long exact sequence includes invariants of \(\widetilde K^*/U\), so both the meaning of “mod \(p\)” and the inherited range \(i>1\) must be settled before the margin can be answered.''',r'''The supplied context gives no answer to this coefficient question; scan 048’s \(G/U\) argument supplies an internal parallel, with the same exact-sequence boundary identified in N077.''',[],flags=['self'])
add('N089','J. The final Tsen and coefficient-comparison leaf','A nonzero cocycle killed by the coefficient inclusion',[(51,10),(51,19)],'own idea',r'“un vrai isomorphisme?”',r'H.?1|racines|roots|torsion|Galois|galois',r'''For \(K=\mathbf C(t)\), all roots of unity \(U\) lie in \(K\), and \(c(g)=g(\sqrt t)/\sqrt t\in\mu_2\subset U\) is a continuous nontrivial character of \(G_K\), because the \(t\)-adic valuation shows \(t\) is not a square in \(K\). Every \(U\)-valued coboundary is \(g(u)/u=1\), so \([c]\ne0\) in ordinary \(H^1(K,U)\), but under \(U\hookrightarrow(K^{\mathrm{sep}})^*\) the same cocycle is the coboundary of \(\sqrt t\). Does this exact calculation explain why the corrected degree range \(i>1\) must be retained, and what additional convention is needed before applying it to the hatted notation?''',r'''No supplied context entry settles this map; the same coefficient inclusion also tests the unqualified degree-one passage on scan 048, giving a direct connection within the current package.''',[],confidence='high for ordinary continuous H1 with discrete coefficients; unresolved for the source’s hatted convention',reason='The cocycle factors through the explicit quadratic extension, and the two coboundary calculations are written out.')
